@title Home-Office Stipend Policy
@subtitle Effective 2027-01-01
@author People Operations, Larkspur Analytics
@date 2027-01-01

Working from home should be comfortable and set up properly. This page explains who gets the home-office stipend, what it covers and how to claim it.

kpi Setup stipend | $500 | one-time, renews after 3 years
kpi Monthly allowance | $40 | internet and phone
kpi Claim window | 60 days | from purchase
kpi Reimbursement | 10 business days | or sooner

## Who is covered

- Every employee who works from home at least 3 days a week.
- You become eligible after 90 days of service.
- Part-time employees receive 50 percent of each amount.

## What you get

table = benefit,full-time,part-time,how often; Setup stipend,$500,$250,Once every 3 years; Internet and phone,$40,$20,Every month

You can use the setup stipend again once 3 years have passed since you first used it.

## What you can buy

The setup stipend covers:

- A desk
- A chair
- A monitor
- A keyboard
- A headset
- Lighting

## How to claim

1. If anything costs more than $250, get written approval from your manager before you buy it.
2. Buy what you need and keep the receipts.
3. Submit the receipts in the expense portal within 60 days of purchase.
4. Your reimbursement arrives within 10 business days.

! Purchases over $250 need your manager's written approval before you buy, not after.

## What is not covered

- Gaming equipment
- Furniture for non-work use
- Software subscriptions
- Anything the company already supplies

---

Questions? Write to [finance-help@larkspur.example](mailto:finance-help@larkspur.example) or ask in the `#finance-help` channel.
